[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about dates by subject line. Read by cause, the
reports split into three problems. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser does not close #4471. Two of the three problems survive that fix.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

1. **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
   so day and month swap. Ticket: [renemifsud/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#1](https://github.com/renemifsud/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
2. **hint**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then reads the
   date day first. People type what the hint says. Day and month swap. Ticket:
   [renemifsud/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#2](https://github.com/renemifsud/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
3. **one-day**: some dates show one day early, and the day depends on where the reader is.
   Nothing is swapped. Ticket: [renemifsud/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows#3](https://github.com/renemifsud/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3).

## How the reports were placed

- One id, one report: the export repeats some rows, and they are counted once.
- The cause comes from the tenant and the way in (`causes.ts`), not the subject and not the
  intake tag.
- A report the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) counts under **one-day** as the
  desk reads it, and stays counted where it is filed by tenant, as the desk's own table does.

## What to change in triage

Subject lines do not tell causes apart ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
The same subject turns up in all three problems. Check the tenant, the form and the way in
before merging.

